WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.817 --> 00:00:06.113
- Tyler ran into a brick wall.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.423
- [Tyler] I don't know.

00:00:09.423 --> 00:00:11.260
- I don't know, when you
look at the instant replay,

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.960
I think you moved more than I did.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.283
You've got more perspective.

00:00:19.372 --> 00:00:21.772
I just wanna be happy,
don't you wanna be happy?

00:00:25.106 --> 00:00:27.689
(upbeat music)

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.020
Just went through a Snap Back workout.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.130
Snap Back, brand new
company we're working with

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.610
at Vayner Sports, bunch of Vayner Sports,

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.290
NFL athletes, the team.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.190
It's fucking hard.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.779
I have an idea, I have another idea.

00:02:45.779 --> 00:02:47.763
Do you wanna do the Malbec tomorrow?

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.570
- How do you manage that many pots or hats

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.930
and try to give your attention to

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.570
all the different endeavors--

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.773
- I have a really good answer for that.

00:02:58.773 --> 00:03:00.951
- But yet not neglecting
something that's so important.

00:03:00.951 --> 00:03:01.784
How does that happen?

00:03:01.784 --> 00:03:03.410
'Cause I know that's a
question that I'm asked a lot,

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.258
and how do you balance that?

00:03:05.258 --> 00:03:07.480
- For me, I think I put 70 to 80%

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.040
of my pure mental energy
to the core thing,

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.590
which is Vayner Media.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.610
Vayner Media is the biggest
company of them all,

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.578
it's the engine.

00:03:15.578 --> 00:03:18.100
And then the rest of the 20%,

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.530
there's a really interesting
thing that an entrepreneur,

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:23.680
that he or she needs to be
able to manage a lot of things,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.890
which is, I'll use this analogy T.D.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.300
This is the easiest way I can put it.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.350
Some people really just
wanna juggle three balls,

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.140
and they do it, and nothing
falls, and they're like, "Look."

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.830
And I'm like, "Cool, that's amazing."

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:39.103
I'm gonna juggle 25 plates,
nine of them are gonna break.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.640
But I'm 16 to your three.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.109
And because I actually
don't care about judgment,

00:03:45.109 --> 00:03:46.570
because where people...

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.800
The reason a lot of
people don't do things is,

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.130
look, Empathy, which is a
wine brand that I launched.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.730
I come from the wine business,

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.120
I'm building a machine
that's building brands,

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.350
and if Empathy fails, that's like a big L,

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:02.040
and like could really like slow me down

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.240
if somebody's thoughtfully looking at me,

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:06.070
but I'm okay with that L.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.870
And I think what you need to do is

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.360
have a stomach to be able to have losses.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:11.980
- Have you had any losses?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:12.950
- Plenty.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.010
You know, when we started Vayner Media,

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.450
I also launched two other companies,

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:19.220
Corked and Forest.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.030
A lot of things I invest in, incubate...

00:04:23.265 --> 00:04:24.443
- [A.J.] Divisions.

00:04:24.443 --> 00:04:25.276
- Here's where things--

00:04:25.276 --> 00:04:26.308
- [A.J.] Failure is part of the team.

00:04:26.308 --> 00:04:27.141
- It has to be.

00:04:27.141 --> 00:04:29.520
- And here's where people
need clarity on this.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:30.944
Micro failures.

00:04:30.944 --> 00:04:32.027
- Right.

00:04:32.027 --> 00:04:33.388
- Not macro.

00:04:33.388 --> 00:04:34.221
- Not the major ones.

00:04:34.221 --> 00:04:36.140
- And this is where people get confused.

00:04:37.301 --> 00:04:39.700
Over the last 10 years of my career

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.280
I've probably lost millions of dollars

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.390
every year on a failure, but nothing--

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:45.360
- You're making me feel
real good right now.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.270
- But the reason I'm making you feel good

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:48.310
and I don't have the details of

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.830
where you're going with that, is,

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.706
but it didn't put you out of business.

00:04:51.706 --> 00:04:53.840
You didn't have to go and be Rocky V

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.446
and go back to like...

00:04:55.446 --> 00:04:57.700
- It's like the sports stuff, though.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.300
I mean it's football,
you're failing every time.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.470
We fail a lot in sports and you try to,

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.420
but every game you fail,
you lose, something happens.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.560
You gotta get up, you
gotta wipe yourself off,

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.040
dust yourself off and
you gotta get back up.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.600
- You know it's funny you bring that up.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.760
Sports and business, A.J.
you have a great quote,

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:13.640
what did you say the other day,

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.390
fits major sport or something.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:16.730
I thought that was super smart,

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:17.563
what was it exactly?

00:05:17.563 --> 00:05:18.500
- Just the concept that you know,

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.160
there's four major sports in our country,

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.950
debatable which of the four are the four,

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.400
but business in itself
is the fifth major sport.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.710
And I think there's a reason why

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:27.550
so many athletes gravitate
towards business,

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:30.140
because for me, my favorite
part about Vayner Sports

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.790
is the competitive landscape.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.320
I love just competing.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.490
And I didn't have the physical gifts

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:37.450
or the work ethic to
do it in a real sport,

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.240
so to speak, or a quantified sport,

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.180
but business gives me that outlet.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.843
- Nice to meet you, take care.

00:05:42.843 --> 00:05:44.724
Take care, everyone.

00:05:44.724 --> 00:05:47.391
(melodic music)

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:53.810
About to go to the Vayner
Sports networking event,

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.373
doing a chat with TI.

00:05:57.182 --> 00:05:58.670
And we're really looking forward to it.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:05:59.503
Yeah!

00:05:59.503 --> 00:06:00.443
I would like that.

00:06:00.443 --> 00:06:01.840
So that's what we're doing.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.580
Just did a podcast with Terrell Davis,

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:07.813
former Bronco great that
broke my heart in '98.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.080
So, that was mixed feelings.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.610
Never really hated him, he's a good dude.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:17.200
Let's go.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.300
- [Female] Here.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.133
- Right here?

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:21.220
You're welcome.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:22.350
- Since the last time I saw you

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.520
you've dropped some new sneakers.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.353
- I did.

00:06:24.353 --> 00:06:25.186
- You have some cards with tops.

00:06:25.186 --> 00:06:26.019
- I do.

00:06:26.019 --> 00:06:26.950
- You're in e-sports now.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:27.783
- Yes.

00:06:27.783 --> 00:06:28.830
- What's next?

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.430
- What's next, what have we not announced?

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:34.040
You know, the reality is both
the tops, sports card insert,

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:38.044
the ownership in the
Call of Duty franchise,

00:06:38.044 --> 00:06:40.530
with the Wilfs from the Vikings.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.970
Everything can move very fast
when you have a macro plan.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.840
Neither of those two things
were even on the radar

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.461
when I saw you in Atlanta.

00:06:48.461 --> 00:06:51.230
And so when I hear the
question what's next,

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:54.650
the reality is it's a
framework of being ready

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:58.132
to move on something tomorrow
if that email comes in

00:06:58.132 --> 00:07:01.180
or that dinner happens and it seems right.

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.089
So I think of myself far
more as a counter puncher

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:07.010
or a halftime adjustments head coach

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:09.463
than the one that works all week or plans.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.150
I have one business objective,

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.530
to buy the New York Jets.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.010
When I consumer information
and opportunities,

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:19.490
if I feel like that can advance
it, whether it's financial,

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:21.600
like a big investment
or starting a company,

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.070
or whether it's just optically.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.613
Like the tops deal is a money loser

00:07:25.613 --> 00:07:27.900
for what I'm getting from tops,

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.680
but it continues to penetrate me

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.020
into the sports consciousness,

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.010
which gives me leverage in the long term.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.840
So some of it's brand,
some of it's dollars,

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:40.820
but what's next is the
continuation of a framework

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.850
that allows me to respond
quickly to an opportunity

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.383
that I think is viable.

00:07:48.335 --> 00:07:50.380
- The best words I could come up with

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.280
is stop making excuses for yourself,

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.500
there's nothing holding you back

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.700
from doing what you wanna do but you.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.323
Stop looking for somebody
to change your life.

00:07:59.639 --> 00:08:01.810
I mean to be honest with you,
- Truth.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.570
us, in whatever industry,

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.560
respective industries that we're in,

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:08.590
it's our job to identify you.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:11.160
So if you continue to work hard,

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:12.720
you don't have to introduce yourself,

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.081
I'm gonna come find you.

00:08:14.081 --> 00:08:14.914
- 100%.

00:08:14.914 --> 00:08:16.940
- All you gotta do is continue to let

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:19.860
your efforts and energy speak for itself.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.830
And eventually it's gonna happen.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:24.440
If it doesn't happen
in association with me,

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.918
maybe I wasn't the one for the job.

00:08:26.918 --> 00:08:29.620
(applause)

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.629
We all have something special,

00:08:31.629 --> 00:08:35.150
a special gift, talent,
something to contribute,

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:38.450
that nobody else can
give the world but you.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:39.283
- True.

00:08:39.283 --> 00:08:41.841
Just to build on that,
just your own perspective.

00:08:41.841 --> 00:08:43.840
People hear you've got your own talent

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.330
and then people are like
fuck, I don't have a,

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.600
like I don't really.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:49.320
But perspective, everyone's
got their two cents,

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.270
and angles matter on this shit.

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.890
So I'll just leave with this.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.290
Action always wins.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.535
Right this second we're in a room

00:08:57.535 --> 00:08:59.689
filled with a ton of interesting people.

00:08:59.689 --> 00:09:02.114
What's about to actually happen

00:09:02.114 --> 00:09:04.190
is everyone's gonna go into their normal

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.438
fucking clique that they came with

00:09:06.438 --> 00:09:09.670
and not meet one or two new people.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:14.492
So my parting gift is please
say hello to two random people

00:09:14.492 --> 00:09:17.345
that you have no fucking
idea who they are,

00:09:17.345 --> 00:09:20.320
and I promise you you'll get
some value out of tonight.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.153
- [Male] Let's go!

00:09:21.153 --> 00:09:22.762
- Thank you for coming.

